{"step_index":1269,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:49:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:33+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:33+08:00\nThe search for \"Firestore REST API list collection query documents orderBy mask fields vanilla JS\" returned the following summary:\nTo query a collection using the **Cloud Firestore REST API** with Vanilla JavaScript (`fetch`), you need to use the `runQuery` endpoint via a **`POST`** request[1][2]. \n\nTo accomplish **filtering fields (Mask/Projection)**, **ordering (`orderBy`)**, and targeting a collection, you construct a `structuredQuery` object in the request body[3][4][5].\n\n### Vanilla JavaScript Example\n\n```javascript\nasync function queryFirestoreDocuments() {\n  const projectId = \"YOUR_PROJECT_ID\";\n  const databaseId = \"(default)\"; // usually (default)\n  const collectionName = \"users\"; // your collection\n  \n  // Optional: If your Firestore rules require authentication, pass a Bearer token\n  const authToken = \"YOUR_FIREBASE_AUTH_TOKEN\"; \n\n  // Endpoint for running structured queries\n  const url = `https://firestore.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${projectId}/databases/${databaseId}/documents:runQuery`;\n\n  // Construct the Structured Query payload\n  const requestBody = {\n    structuredQuery: {\n      // 1. Specify the collection to query\n      from: [{ collectionId: collectionName }],\n\n      // 2. Mask/Projection: Return only specific fields to reduce payload size\n      select: {\n        fields: [\n          { fieldPath: \"fullName\" },\n          { fieldPath: \"email\" }\n        ]\n      },\n\n      // 3. Order results by a specific field\n      orderBy: [\n        {\n          field: { fieldPath: \"fullName\" },\n          direction: \"ASCENDING\" // or \"DESCENDING\"\n        }\n      ],\n\n      // Optional: Limit number of results\n      limit: 10\n    }\n  };\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(url, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: {\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n        // \"Authorization\": `Bearer ${authToken}` // Uncomment if auth is needed\n      },\n      body: JSON.stringify(requestBody)\n    });\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      const errorData = await response.json();\n      throw new Error(`Error: ${errorData.error.message}`);\n    }\n\n    const data = await response.json();\n    \n    // Parse and print results\n    data.forEach((item, index) => {\n      if (item.document) {\n        const docPath = item.document.name; // Full resource path\n        const fields = item.document.fields;  // Your masked fields\n        \n        console.log(`Document ${index + 1} (${docPath}):`, {\n          fullName: fields.fullName?.stringValue,\n          email: fields.email?.stringValue\n        });\n      }\n    });\n\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Failed to execute query:\", error);\n  }\n}\n\n// Run the function\nqueryFirestoreDocuments();\n```\n\n### Key Payload Properties Explained:\n1. **`from`**: Specifies the target collection layout. `collectionId` takes the name of your Firestore collection[6][5].\n2. **`select` (Field Mask)**: Acts as a projection mask[3]. By defining `fields`, you instruct Firestore to only return the specified keys (`fullName`, `email`), omitting everything else[5].\n3. **`orderBy`**: Accepts an array of sorting criteria[3]. Each rule requires a `fieldPath` and a `direction` (`ASCENDING` or `DESCENDING`). *Note: Ensure you have matching indexes created in your Firebase Console if sorting combined with inequality filters.*\n4. **Response Format**: Firestore returns an array of objects[1]. Each matched document is wrapped inside an object (`item.document`), containing the raw typed values (e.g., `stringValue`, `integerValue`, `booleanValue`).\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEObZOD5mwY73zDEk_wz9_4MDSO-9AIwCxMys45weuAeWOv0tDYN4P_MatEVuYpUgBNbCkAX2jYSSNS56HAPys0GlQxNOh1jwNjq5KGP4i4BOGQT0awujvkEZ4kQFrgE9odj-AMdH9XyjCp5gYMvQ8bVrhTYGY28WEWprzAogXg6ufRwSphUEz0w_KaV0MWpwUilSpiAbRldWTF__n3)\n[2] [gitbook.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEXO2i_3ah7hISJJXhwlpjx9Ba-FMkEHCDMfExW7uYRL4jGBBGQDgwvDSUh1MQXcT72IHKZLT8Iaryucxu0U027YajNgYY-yib0UBwe3WGzfH5JPedy_v9hJ0EsWQgHY7UoNkzF1CMAomJDF58z)\n[3] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHwlTbSj0_jsGJO2HqgkMFoUQWZjTYvbC2asuWoJKKXByDYECe5k4itfiODqjH0c2WYBhHQi-9RfRQU7yFYtzlZ60C-FVeRjjMti2PdK5-TP5lQ2JprsPqGgYdDNtbHmrtLFKpLsKjUY1sqnIrh-rXOnNXiKcdblMquF3TwZo0BN4KPLH-pmJw=)\n[4] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHrhEu2rAv201NTfL49vZsRJLmKUv4Pc_90Eqly3ue3VxrFJr15V_XCGaY9jSgplbUziGb3uVkTPhclHV-gTEP9jwjmknz_WK44HJvK75-NJ6FXlO6obf4yPAhBcDwNVP06PohxcNleJF79EaZYTRXJX3GQVRbhhvtwzg-6YO30eBwO)\n[5] [gitbook.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEXO2i_3ah7hISJJXhwlpjx9Ba-FMkEHCDMfExW7uYRL4jGBBGQDgwvDSUh1MQXcT72IHKZLT8Iaryucxu0U027YajNgYY-yib0UBwe3WGzfH5JPedy_v9hJ0EsWQgHY7UoNkzF1CMAomJDF58z)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEG646nMctsNqrsKcqRoWyFIHTDYC7n74qhUTJpnROd-d_94eC50kWsV9vn3_Dlbvq50q_IijvHS1aHSgARSbSxcUmiEVAEF92GHK526J9agzQInWG3EWMQCSprkgWOoLGhJVeJLP2l3Pk55ImCymmzbLIHTsCX-iHg-x9m1kPEmLsbXdMXIXxwgwqavubhLuxFCRVscxa6bEd52mXZycCxwadn)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":1270,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:49:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:37+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:49:25+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:49:37+08:00\nThe search for \"HTML5 anchor download filename sanitization Windows reserved characters vanilla JS\" returned the following summary:\nWhen building client-side file downloads using vanilla JavaScript and the HTML5 `download` attribute (`<a href=\"...\" download=\"filename\">`), user-provided or dynamically generated strings can easily break downloads or cause security issues on Windows machines[1][2]. \n\nWindows file systems disallow specific **reserved characters**, **control codes**, **device names** (like `CON`, `NUL`, `COM1`), and **trailing periods/spaces**[3][4][5].\n\nHere is a robust, production-ready vanilla JavaScript helper function to thoroughly sanitize filenames for cross-platform safety (with a heavy focus on Windows limitations):\n\n### Vanilla JS Sanitization Function\n\n```javascript\nfunction sanitizeFilename(input, replacement = '_') {\n  if (typeof input !== 'string') return 'download';\n\n  // 1. Control characters (0x00–0x1f and 0x80–0x9f)\n  const controlRe = /[\\x00-\\x1f\\x80-\\x9f]/g;\n  \n  // 2. Windows reserved characters: < > : \" / \\ | ? *\n  const reservedCharsRe = /[<>:\"/\\\\|?*]/g;\n  \n  // 3. Windows reserved device names (CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1-9, LPT1-9) with optional extension\n  const windowsReservedRe = /^(con|prn|aux|nul|com[1-9]|lpt[1-9])(\\..*)?$/i;\n  \n  // 4. Unix hidden files or relative paths if stripped poorly (optional safeguard for just dots)\n  const leadingTrailingDotsSpacesRe = /^[. ]+|[. ]+$/g;\n\n  let sanitized = input\n    .replace(controlRe, replacement)\n    .replace(reservedCharsRe, replacement)\n    .trim();\n\n  // Handle Windows reserved device names by prefixing them if matched\n  if (windowsReservedRe.test(sanitized)) {\n    sanitized = replacement + sanitized;\n  }\n\n  // Strip leading/trailing dots and spaces (Windows drops/malfunctions with these)\n  sanitized = sanitized.replace(leadingTrailingDotsSpacesRe, '');\n\n  // Fallback if string became completely empty\n  if (!sanitized || sanitized === '') {\n    sanitized = 'download';\n  }\n\n  // Truncate to safe byte/character length (Windows max filename length is typically 255 chars)\n  return sanitized.slice(0, 255);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to use it with an HTML5 Anchor Tag (`<a>`)\n\nYou can combine this function with a Blob or a local data/object URL to trigger a safe, programmatic download in vanilla JavaScript:\n\n```javascript\nfunction triggerDownload(userProvidedName, fileContent, mimeType = 'text/plain') {\n  // 1. Sanitize the filename\n  const safeName = sanitizeFilename(userProvidedName);\n\n  // 2. Create a Blob from the content\n  const blob = new Blob([fileContent], { type: mimeType });\n  const blobUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n\n  // 3. Create dynamic anchor element\n  const anchor = document.createElement('a');\n  anchor.href = blobUrl;\n  anchor.download = safeName; // HTML5 download attribute\n\n  // 4. Append to DOM, click to fire download, then clean up\n  document.body.appendChild(anchor);\n  anchor.click();\n  \n  document.body.removeChild(anchor);\n  URL.revokeObjectURL(blobUrl);\n}\n\n// --- Example Usage ---\n// This will clean out invalid characters like '?', ':', and spaces, \n// and safely handle the Windows reserved word \"CON\".\ntriggerDownload('CON?report:2026.txt', 'Here is the report data.');\n// Resulting downloaded file: \"_CON_report_2026.txt\"\n```\n\n### Key Rules Handled by This Sanitizer:\n1. **Windows Restricted Symbols:** Strips out `<`, `>`, `:`, `\"`, `/`, `\\`, `|`, `?`, and `*`[3][5][6].\n2. **ASCII Control Codes:** Removes invisible or layout-breaking control characters (`0x00` to `0x1F`)[3][4].\n3. **Windows Reserved Words:** Detects names like `CON`, `NUL`, `AUX`, `COM1`, etc. (case-insensitive) and prefixes them so Windows doesn't reject the file write[3][4].\n4. **Trailing/Leading Spaces & Periods:** Prevents file creation glitches on NTFS formatting by stripping edge spaces and dots (`.`)[4][5].\n5. **Length Restriction:** Caps the filename at 255 characters to abide by standard OS file system limits[3][4].\n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFhfX5agtYz6IQB7Go6i9d24SrWBcOOp2cCYtI4xVxUXXMKO9FEoscMZ6hfrg83XuBKPTly5gCOCRkmR9DVW_IrJUTsisPYPCcf-YgXCR8CRVmpfX-ZR_OakhyqQjMd8XOR0Sw94Db8R7pZWktGra6BDGpKt7zpX-iAy-uid361OPvbZQw58izNOiVfISwlrxWi)\n[2] [jonathancrozier.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzwfh9fP7osDoYPt8-t4iyKLExbegUDyVVmgP-jk5OsG7f-FG00xp-VQN3q80a1d6_95eFhBpJL7NIuXCl3VSNOp0M5ZSjWgbEsLJfnbu_bX6srVb-2UhptQtdMMNOWoRJFYfaHTBDeQn4ppC6JQ21zpTPotwmm6PmmaxpOldpSORE7oa3uXlOA64_5SC0FTZYLdvCU3I=)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGqBgmrtaIeQXYGwiOJZWJbMbk1lOxFbArkHunV9FX8tl1P3BizFx2NZZJT5_hNeSMHHSvICMnN8nX3HLacuC_ZVtC-t7K-WmwhWwbwsCX-xHEf1IjFRdVAYCv6kXyfxdHuOw==)\n[4] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFSbQ24hWkZTn_Z5YhIitFbedqPauLujO3rgVd2spIgKKe_5TxSuqUpqT1Z544ttiHGp9WtYatp8Sf8ysvkF89Q1NFFVkh6vOBC0R0ZxkEVuVuh1E191g52jMOZSMiMptzcMAQv8Q==)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHHcvJD7-r019AXEdogV_bWYnDTSrgpeyOB64ID7dFZEIL3lfSvCGLk6ga19TRJrtQ1SjWMKyV3Q4jzgnSRfSbNKA82C2odd6Db97XhqWF1iTOB9vcAMJLt51uUPjOqmcu1tKOPbaxDwrD5G-t4kvFS4SqLqaOKGKNRsuznTkxX3I4WHgLg6hg8C-8GQLYpBwka4kOYDaekhU4maAjGsHyP3yCbA==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEcwjZ_fYadyY1yRF0yL0zmKPufSQVapmI2diS1T62V33hAFrMW07zmXuw-9LUBcITfmy5wxrBuBAWuGAD1MPiLixbwlmGEZjYwV6XeysMpA-aGJkLiDHgskw-VROUXxhSw4dtaK5rq9wKMRbalsZC054npujlpm7kwRXoKZGLJTs3NSeyOTlf_aSm_VT0fcW3zXF1J5r7ojLE-y_3mrjyio1-Qub2a)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
